<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Toco narrows year loss.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Toco narrows year loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline loss	 13	    vs 115</p>
<p>    - attrib loss	   28	    vs 116</p>
<p>    Attrib loss	     31.75	 vs 116.60</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss	    12.87	 vs 113.09</p>
<p>    Tax			 2.13	  vs 2.06</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   21.21	 vs 14.32</p>
<p>    Turnover		  249.40	vs 199.77</p>
<p>    Exceptional loss	17.12	 vs 0.01</p>
<p>Full name: Toco Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Industrial firm Toco said a radical restructuring now meant most of the group's trading units were operating satisfactorily with strong prospects of recording substantial earnings increases in the short to medium-term.</p>
<p>Toco said it was confident it could return to profitability by the end of the next financial year.</p>
<p>Toco added that the process of evaluating core activities and looking for further possible disposals was continuing.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
